theory.intro:
A **segment** is the region between a chord and the arc it cuts off. A minor segment's area is the sector area minus the area of the triangle formed by the two radii. For the minor-segment formula and the corresponding major-segment complement, use the minor central angle $0<\theta\leq\pi$. The segment-perimeter formula below is for the minor segment. Work in radians throughout.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (60:3);
\coordinate (B) at (-60:3);
\fill[gray!35] (B) arc (-60:60:3) -- cycle;
\draw (O) circle (3);
\draw[thick] (O) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (B) node[midway, below left] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.8cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=B--O--A};
\node[above right] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
